  notes:"<p class=\"intro-lead\">If you're here, it's because you want to discover the DC Multiverse, or watch one of its branches, in its most optimized order, a mix of chronological order and release order. You'll find extra details by clicking on each media, and this entire site is guaranteed free of major spoilers.</p><div class=\"intro-tags\"><span class=\"itag\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M20 6 9 17l-5-5\"/></svg>This guide works for first-time watches as well as rewatches.</span></div><p class=\"intro-note\">Fair warning: this section is a <strong>huge mess</strong>. Even though a lot of media has been cut, watching everything that's left still takes a lot — a LOT — of time. If you're only here for the Arrowverse, the DCEU or the DCU, you can pick below by unchecking what you don't want to see.</p><div class=\"intro-qa\"><p class=\"q\">Fair question: how is this whole mess connected?</p><p class=\"a\">This order favors a progressive discovery of the DC Multiverse. Several shows and movies take place in different realities but end up sharing connections. Watching everything in this order helps you understand the characters, references and events that tie these universes together, while preserving the major surprises.</p></div><div class=\"keys-title\">How to read this</div><div class=\"keys\"><div class=\"key\"><div class=\"key-h\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"9\"/><path d=\"M3 12h18M12 3c2.5 3 2.5 15 0 18M12 3c-2.5 3-2.5 15 0 18\"/></svg>The main chronologies</div><p>The universe's two main chronologies take place on <strong>Earth-Prime</strong> and <strong>Earth-1</strong>.</p></div><div class=\"key\"><div class=\"key-h\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M10 13a5 5 0 0 0 7 0l2-2a5 5 0 0 0-7-7l-1 1\"/><path d=\"M14 11a5 5 0 0 0-7 0l-2 2a5 5 0 0 0 7 7l1-1\"/></svg>Soft-canon</div><p>The term <strong>soft-canon</strong> refers to media whose events partly happened the same way in another universe — more info in the descriptions.</p></div><div class=\"key\"><div class=\"key-h\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M11 19 2 12l9-7v14zM22 19l-9-7 9-7v14z\"/></svg>Flashbacks</div><p>Some events work better as a <strong>FLASHBACK</strong> for understanding, and are marked as such.</p></div><div class=\"key wide\"><div class=\"key-h\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><circle cx=\"9\" cy=\"9\" r=\"4\"/><path d=\"M2 21a7 7 0 0 1 14 0M17 6a4 4 0 0 1 0 8M22 21a7 7 0 0 0-4-6.3\"/></svg>Duplicate faces</div><p>The DC Multiverse works in a peculiar way: two different characters can have the exact same face (examples: Flash's father (2014) and Flash (1990), Supergirl (1984) and Superman's mother (Smallville) but also Supergirl's adoptive mother (2015)).</p></div></div><details class=\"cuts\"><summary>What's left out, and why<span class=\"n\">4 entries</span><svg class=\"chev\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m6 9 6 6 6-6\"/></svg></summary><div class=\"cuts-body\"><p class=\"cuts-intro\">Some media is intentionally left out because it's not at all important for understanding the Multiverse's chronology and its key events.</p><dl class=\"cuts-list\"><div class=\"cut\"><dt>Everything released before 1989</dt><dd>Every media released before 1989.</dd></div><div class=\"cut\"><dt>The shows</dt><dd>Flash (1990), Lois &amp; Clark, Lucifer, Pennyworth, Swamp-Thing, Doom Patrol, Powerless, Birds of Prey (2002).</dd></div><div class=\"cut\"><dt>The movies</dt><dd>Constantine (2005), the Watchmen movie and show, both Joker movies, the Green Lantern movie, the Catwoman movie.</dd></div><div class=\"cut\"><dt>The rest</dt><dd>Plenty of other lesser-known movies and shows, almost every animated movie and show, every comic, every video game.</dd></div></dl></div></details>",
  crisis:"<div class=\"crisis-content\">\n      <div class=\"crisis-block\">\n<details class=\"crisis-spoil\">\n          <summary>⚠️ Reveal the details — SPOILERS</summary>\n          <div class=\"crisis-spoil-content\">\n            This is <strong>Crisis on Infinite Earths</strong>, the biggest crossover in all of DC history. The entire Multiverse is rebooted from scratch — some realities disappear, others are merged. Dozens of characters from dozens of DC movies and shows across the franchise's entire history make cameos. It's an unprecedented event.<br><br>\n            <strong>Episodes:</strong><br>\n            Arrow — Season 8 Episode 8<br>\n            The Flash — Season 6 Episode 9<br>\n            Supergirl — Season 5 Episode 9<br>\n            Batwoman — Season 1 Episode 9<br>\n            Legends of Tomorrow — Season 5 Episode 1\n          </div>\n        </details>\n      </div>\n    </div>",
